WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.342
On this slide, we are focusing on parentheses control calculation order.

00:00:04.342 --> 00:00:09.632
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.632 --> 00:00:15.847
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.847 --> 00:00:20.177
Parentheses make the intended calculation order explicit.

00:00:20.177 --> 00:00:27.012
Code can run without an error and still be analytically wrong if the formula is grouped incorrectly.

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:30.187
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:35.257
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:40.282
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:40.282 --> 00:00:42.714
from the names and output.
